  "description": "its main frame made this\nyear from Fuji's new X-Fusion Alpha tubes. Like 853 steel, X-Fusion resists\nweakening from the heat of the welding torch. A strong tube can be made\nthin and light. By careful choice of tube size and thickness, a frame\ncan be made to ride gracefully over the road. Like a well-suspended car,\nnot a buckboard.\n\nRoubaix parts are fine Shimano 105 for the most part, except for the very\ncool Ritchey Pro wheels. The Roubaix crankset is a 105 triple: 27 gears,\nseveral of them lower than any gear on an 18-gear bike. If you like to\nspin the pedals up long grades or if you do big miles in hilly country,\nyou'll love that third chainring. You may have the same riding objectives\nwe mentioned in the Roubaix Pro story. We think you might chose a Roubaix\nover a Roubaix Pro because you preferred the X-Fusion frame and the gearing.\n\nYou'd chose a Roubaix because you like X-Fusion's response, as if every\nbit of effort you put into the pedals moved you instantly forward on the\nroad. You'd also like that third chainring, which frankly wouldn't matter\nmuch riding across Ohio. But maybe you're crossing Colorado...",
